===Golden Skin Strategies===
*'''For the first quest''', play normally until you see {{CI|Twisted Ribecca|name=true}} on the [[Floor]]. Then, either encounter her normally or ask the distractor to bring Twisted Ribecca to the [[Elevator]].
*'''For the second quest''', play normally until you encounter an [[Ichor Leak]]. Then, walk through as many puddles as you can find. If it's not enough, go to the next [[Floor]] and hope you get one, as those will have a higher chance of appearing. You should also avoid {{CDI|Piping Tape|name=true}}, as that can make it take longer to find Ichor leaks.
*'''For the third quest''', just play normally, reaching the [[Halloween Floor]] if possible. You should die at Floor 10/15, as the game will take longer, making the quest take longer than if you just redid another run.
==Strategies==
Ribecca is a great All-Rounder [[Toon]] for runs, as her Passive [[Ability]], '''The Undead''', bypasses all applied [[Debuffs]], such as {{CI|Twisted Vee|name=true}}'s {{Debuff|Slow|II}} Debuff applied on a chase; {{CI|Twisted Astro|name=true}}'s {{Debuff|Tired|III}} Debuff; {{Debuff|Illness|III}}, {{Debuff|Slow|I}}, and Ichor Stains from [[Ichor Leak]] Puddles being a few examples. This makes the above [[Twisteds]] along with any other Debuff sources almost to fully non-threats. Being easily accessible during the [[Halloween Event]], Ribecca is a great option for starters who struggle with Debuffs.

When she normally would be afflicted with a Debuff, Ribecca gets a 10% boost to a random [[Stat]] for 10 seconds instead. The buff granted is indicated by the color of the particles (and boost ring if enabled) Ribecca gains. Below are the buffs that she can gain and their colors:
*{{Color|'''Orange - Skill Check'''|#C89363}} (Increases chance & size only) (35% chance and 165 size)
*{{Color|'''Yellow - Movement Speed'''|#CFCE6E}} (16.5 Walk Speed/27.5 Run Speed)
*{{Color|'''Green - Stamina'''|#7BCA6B}} (Increases Stamina regeneration only) (2.64/s and 26.4 Stamina regenerated in 10 seconds)
*{{Color|'''Blue - Stealth'''|#6891CA}} (16.5 Stealth)
*{{Color|'''Purple - Extraction Speed'''|#7E56C9}} (1.10 Extraction Speed (~40.9 seconds))

While Ribecca is intended to be a starter Toon and has a really good Passive, you may want to get used to dealing with Debuffs early on as a different Toon. This is because if a starter uses Ribecca for the most part, they may struggle a bit more with Debuffs due to not being used to them when they transition to a different Toon. However, this mostly depends on how you want to progress in the game, so you are still free to play whatever Toon and playstyle you wish. Just remember that it's a good idea to learn how to counter Debuffs by base, especially if you plan to distract at some point as you progress and get more Toons.

Despite the seemingly lacking Ability for more experienced players, Ribecca is actually quite decent in long runs. With the increased likelihood of {{Type|Main}} Twisteds, she can easily handle Twisted Vee and Twisted Astro, being able to pass them to distractors or pull them away from teammates, all without worrying about the Debuffs. When Twisted Shelly is on the Floor, Ribecca is capable of extracting faster than most other Toons, only being outpaced by Toons with 5{{Star}} [[Extraction Speed]], above average Skill Check in some cases, as well as certain [[Trinkets]]. {{CI|Twisted Finn|name=true}}'s Ichor Puddles can be annoying, especially due to {{CI|Twisted Barnaby|name=true}}, but since Ribecca is immune to the Debuffs, she'll have less of an issue with the effects, and not be bothered much if Twisted Barnaby latches onto her. All of this is before considering the Stat boost she can gain from Debuffs, which can make her even more capable at extracting or defending.

Since she gets a boost from Debuff sources, it could be viable to go out of your way to interact with them. For example, you can go out of your way to extract from {{CI|Twisted Brusha|name=true}}'s vandalized Machines, even for a moment, allowing you to actively give yourself a decent boost.

Ichor Leaks can be dangerous and become more likely the further you go, with Ribecca not being affected by them whatsoever, greatly improving her survivability and extraction capabilities during these Floor Events. In fact, she directly benefits from walking through Ichor Puddles, so don't be afraid to do so, in order to consistently get a Stat boost.

During the [[Easter Event]], [[Spring Fevers]] normally have a significant impact in the form of a constant {{Debuff|Tired|II}}, which would typically make maintaining Stamina a bit difficult, but Ribecca's immunity lets her keep her Stamina in check more easily; she can also reap the benefits of {{Debuff|Energized|II}} with an additional boost too.

As her Ability description states, she isn't immune to negative [[Multipliers]] from Trinkets (such as {{TI|Cooler|name=true}}'s speed decrease), so Trinkets and [[Items]] will still need to be used to remedy or counteract such cases.

Since there's only three Debuff sources that can spawn on [[Dyle's Floor]] (four during the [[Halloween Event]]); Ichor Leaks, Twisted Brusha, and Treadmill Machines (as well as [[Trick or Treat Doors]]); Ribecca isn't the most reliable for seeking {{CI|Twisted Dyle|name=true}}, as her Stats are average and don't lead to her being able to extract any Machine types particularly quickly. When an Ichor Leak does occur though, she does have an advantage, since the Illness that would usually make missing Skill Checks (and by extension, enraging Twisted Dyle) becomes a Stat boost when she walks through them, albeit this has a slim chance of happening, especially if {{CDI|TIME'S UP|name=true}} is selected on an early Floor. With Twisted Brusha, it's dependent on her spawning, which isn't guaranteed but when she does spawn, the immunity to her graffiti allows Ribecca to extract at a normal pace, with the Stat boost given by extracting from vandalized Machines. Treadmill Machines on the other hand are not an option unless you have {{TI|Mime Makeup|name=true}} equipped, as Ribecca is immune to the speed reduction from failing Treadmill Machine Skill Checks, yet failing a Skill Check will usually enrage Twisted Dyle unless you have the aforementioned Trinket. Trick or Treat Doors only show up during the Halloween Event, and only have a chance to give a Trick that inflicts a Debuff, or the "No Bones About It!" Treat, which empowers Ribecca without needing to interact with a Debuff source; Trick or Treat Doors can make her a little more capable for Dyle Runs, but the randomness isn't reliable.

Her 3 Stars in all Stats means she doesn't have any specific strengths nor weaknesses, so you can usually select Trinkets and focus on collecting Items that best revolve around your playstyle or mitigate your personal weaknesses. Her Ability's boosts can stack with some Trinkets, so that can also be taken into account.

With all of that being said, she can be a pretty decent solo Toon, as Debuffs can be much more impactful when you have no teammates to help you, mitigate the effects, or remove Debuff sources; this isn't to mention her Stat boost from combatting Debuffs. Her Stats may be average across the board, but her lack of needing {{TI|Train Whistle|name=true}} (a common choice for long solo runs) allows her to invest in a different Trinket.

